# ESP32-S3 RS485 Sensor UI (LVGL + Modbus)

This project reads temperature and humidity data from an RS485 sensor (Modbus RTU protocol) using ESP32-S3, then displays the values on an LVGL user interface (labels + arcs).

---

## ⚙️ Hardware Setup

| Component | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| MCU | ESP32-S3 (tested on ESP32-S3-WROOM) |
| Sensor | XY-MD02 (SHT20 inside, Modbus RTU) |
| Interface | RS485 (via MAX485 module) |
| TX Pin | GPIO 20 |
| RX Pin | GPIO 19 |
| Baud Rate | 9600 (8N1) |

Make sure the **A/B lines** on the RS485 module are not swapped — otherwise, the sensor will not respond.

---

## 🧩 Software Overview

### Key Files
- `XY_MD02_Config.h` → contains Modbus setup, data parsing, and UI update function  
- `main.cpp` → initializes UART, LVGL, and periodically calls the update function

---

## 🧠 Main Concepts

### 1️⃣ Avoid Blocking the UI
The standard ModbusMaster library is *blocking*.  
If you call it too frequently or inside LVGL timers, the UI will **freeze or reset**.

To prevent this:
- Use **`millis()` timing** instead of `delay()`
- Never call `node.readInputRegisters()` inside LVGL callbacks
- Keep Modbus reading in the **main loop** (core 1)

### 2️⃣ Non-Blocking Update Function

```cpp
void UpdateRS485(unsigned long updateTime,
                 lv_obj_t* lblTemp, lv_obj_t* lblHumi,
                 lv_obj_t* arcTemp, lv_obj_t* arcHumi);
This function:

Reads Modbus data every updateTime ms

Updates the temperature and humidity labels

Updates both LVGL arcs

Prints values to Serial Monitor

Example usage:

cpp
Copy code
XYMD02::UpdateRS485(2000, ui_LabelTemp, ui_LabelHumi, ui_ArcTemp, ui_ArcHumi);
3️⃣ LVGL Object Type Safety
Be careful when updating widgets:

lv_label_set_text() → expects string

lv_arc_set_value() → expects integer

Issue	Cause	Fix
UI freezes or ESP resets	Modbus blocking too long	Use millis timing or separate task on same core
LVGL crash on label update	Wrong widget type or NULL pointer	Verify all UI object types and initialization
No data from RS485	TX/RX pins reversed or A/B swapped	Check wiring and 120Ω termination
Serial prints but UI doesn't update	Wrong LVGL update context	Only update inside loop() or after lv_timer_handler()


🧰 Notes
Keep all Modbus operations in the same core as loop() (core 1)

Avoid heavy Modbus operations in LVGL timer callbacks

Always validate object pointers before calling LVGL APIs

Use snprintf() instead of sprintf() for safer string formatting

🧑‍💻 Author Notes
This project started as a debugging test for Modbus and ended up becoming a stable RS485 + LVGL template.
Perfect for quick integration of industrial sensors with embedded UI.